From 13f0dadafeacc2a27dd765274ed105aeae402e0f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hanoip <hanoip@localhost>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 18:21:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 194/194] media: i2c: add Motorola hanoip camera sensor and VCM
 drivers

Drivers for the Moto G60 (hanoip) cameras, register tables generated
from the vendor com.qti.sensormodule bins (decode-regs-v3 /
gen-sensor-tables in the hanoip-mainline repository):

- s5k4h7: rear wide/macro, 3264x2448 RAW10 GRBG, 4 lanes at 366 MHz,
  CCS exposure 0x0202 / frame length 0x0340, init = vendor list 2.
- hanoip-cam: OV32B front (3264x2448 BGGR, 4 lanes, 414 MHz) and
  S5KHM2 rear main (4000x3000 GBRG, C-PHY three trios), one fixed
  30 fps mode each; the S5KHM2 init carries the vendor TnP bursts.
- hanoip-vcm: both rear focus motors at 0x0c, DW9768/DW9800 register
  map, started with the vendor init lists (the mainline dw9768 sequence
  does not move them); per-lens default position.

Sensors register with v4l2_async_register_subdev_sensor(), so the
lens-focus lens is bound and gets its own subdev node.
